  "conclusions": [
    "The shared broker and executor handoff are not throughput bottlenecks: production slot submission costs 0.0035 ms per batch and internal broker residence costs 0.120 ms per position.",
    "Most reported queue time is capacity wait in the receiver channel while both synchronous slots are occupied; moving it into an internal broker queue would not increase throughput.",
    "Two slots keep production inference occupied 97.7% of steady-state wall capacity. One slot leaves device throughput unused, while three slots create severe host and GPU contention.",
    "Explicit input packing and output materialization consume 26.0% of measured production slot time. Session::run consumes 73.9% and still includes runtime overhead and host-device transfers.",
    "Pinned reusable buffers and ONNX I/O binding are the next justified inference optimization; additional actors have little steady-state device-idle time left to recover at 64 actors."
  ]
